1
00:01:31,290 --> 00:01:35,080
EPISODE 5: A SUMMONER'S POTENTIAL

2
00:01:31,790 --> 00:01:33,000
Oh, they're here!

3
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:34,880
Took you long enough to heal up, Rodin!

4
00:01:35,130 --> 00:01:36,880
Sorry to worry you, fellas.

5
00:01:37,380 --> 00:01:39,290
As you can see, I'm fit as a fiddle!

6
00:01:39,710 --> 00:01:42,460
So, the little guy's really tagging along?

7
00:01:42,670 --> 00:01:46,710
Yeah. As I'm sure you've heard,
we're adopting Allen's hunting strategy this time.

8
00:01:47,290 --> 00:01:48,880
But he's only tagging along to watch.

9
00:01:49,250 --> 00:01:51,960
I won't get in the way. Thanks for having me.

10
00:01:52,420 --> 00:01:56,500
Sigh. I wanted to be part of the hunt.

11
00:01:56,920 --> 00:02:00,290
But Dad's such a hardhead. He wouldn't budge.

12
00:02:00,790 --> 00:02:01,790
Oh, well.

13
00:02:02,170 --> 00:02:05,920
The important thing is that we train the newbies
to help the group hunt more boars.

14
00:02:06,460 --> 00:02:08,920
I don't want to see anybody
get hurt like that again.

15
00:02:09,790 --> 00:02:10,710
Mr. Rodin.

16
00:02:11,420 --> 00:02:12,960
I'm sorry about what happened last year.

17
00:02:13,290 --> 00:02:15,750
Please don't cover for me
if anything goes wrong today.

18
00:02:15,750 --> 00:02:18,210
It's no biggie. Focus on your role in the hunt!

19
00:02:18,460 --> 00:02:19,420
Uh, yessir.

20
00:02:20,290 --> 00:02:22,170
Okay! Let's move out!

21
00:02:22,250 --> 00:02:23,250
Right!

22
00:02:34,250 --> 00:02:38,130
My seventh year living as a serf
and I finally get to leave the village.

23
00:02:38,750 --> 00:02:40,500
One small step forward!

24
00:02:43,330 --> 00:02:45,330
Those must be the White Dragon Mountains.

25
00:02:46,670 --> 00:02:52,170
Every fall, the boars leave the foot of the
mountains to come here in search of food.

26
00:02:52,880 --> 00:02:57,130
And legends say that a mythical White Dragon
lives somewhere near the summit.

27
00:02:57,380 --> 00:02:59,750
The fantasy vibes are through the roof!

28
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:02,580
Hey, Allen! You getting cold feet or what?

29
00:03:03,460 --> 00:03:05,130
No way!

30
00:03:08,330 --> 00:03:09,880
Just stick to what we practiced.

31
00:03:10,290 --> 00:03:12,330
Everybody to your posts!

32
00:03:12,460 --> 00:03:13,040
Right!

33
00:03:13,040 --> 00:03:13,630
Okay!

34
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:20,830
Incoming!

35
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:24,330
Okay, yeah, that's terrifying!

36
00:03:24,790 --> 00:03:26,330
Dig in those heels, men!

37
00:03:30,630 --> 00:03:32,130
Hold fast!

38
00:03:33,330 --> 00:03:34,330
Rodin!

39
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:43,790
The bait team lures the boar in.

40
00:03:43,920 --> 00:03:47,500
Then the tank team holds it in place.
And finally, the strike team attacks its vitals.

41
00:03:47,960 --> 00:03:51,000
This is the method my dad and the
others have used to hunt successfully

42
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,670
for over 10 years without any talents!

43
00:03:53,210 --> 00:03:55,170
It's almost time! Please get ready!

44
00:03:55,170 --> 00:03:56,250
S-sure thing!

45
00:03:56,920 --> 00:04:01,130
It was a mistake to count on weenies like them
to tank anything in the first place.

46
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:02,330
Mr. Gerda!

47
00:04:02,670 --> 00:04:04,880
Better not spear me in the ass by mistake!

48
00:04:04,880 --> 00:04:05,790
Y-yessir!

49
00:04:05,960 --> 00:04:10,080
They should only need to attack it
once to gain experience from the battle!

50
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:11,670
Good! Strike now!

51
00:04:18,130 --> 00:04:19,710
I can feel power flowing through me!

52
00:04:20,040 --> 00:04:23,170
Does that mean we overcame a Trial of the Gods?

53
00:04:23,540 --> 00:04:26,000
Oh, thank the Lord!

54
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,130
Sweet! Just as planned!

55
00:04:29,210 --> 00:04:31,170
Sounds like they leveled up.

56
00:04:31,750 --> 00:04:34,920
Since boars are C-rank monsters,
they must have gained a lot of EXP!

57
00:04:35,460 --> 00:04:37,380
How did I make out?

58
00:04:37,630 --> 00:04:39,330
Damn! I got squat!

59
00:04:39,580 --> 00:04:44,920
Ugh. Figures that it doesn't consider me
part of the battle for just standing nearby.

60
00:04:45,080 --> 00:04:45,830
Allen!

61
00:04:46,790 --> 00:04:48,290
Your advice made all the difference!

62
00:04:48,290 --> 00:04:49,290
Thank you!

63
00:04:49,710 --> 00:04:51,710
Great. You're welcome.

64
00:04:52,460 --> 00:04:56,580
This sucks. A victory laced
with the bitter taste of defeat.

65
00:04:57,750 --> 00:05:00,830
Yo, Allen! You coming along on today's hunt?

66
00:05:01,170 --> 00:05:03,130
Yep! I'll be there to watch as usual.

67
00:05:03,500 --> 00:05:07,790
But do me a favor. Tell my dad
he should let me try wielding a spear, too!

68
00:05:07,880 --> 00:05:11,580
No can do. Rodin would kick our butts
for even suggesting it.

69
00:05:11,790 --> 00:05:15,210
I'm jealous. Wish I could join the hunt, too.

70
00:05:15,210 --> 00:05:17,960
Then put down your butcher's knife for once
and tag along.

71
00:05:17,960 --> 00:05:21,210
Not when my wife's got a kid in her belly!

72
00:05:21,210 --> 00:05:23,960
I've gotta play it safe for her sake.

73
00:05:23,960 --> 00:05:24,670
Fair.

74
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:28,630
But I'm always happy to have
more monster meat to carve up!

75
00:05:28,830 --> 00:05:30,040
Oh?

76
00:05:30,630 --> 00:05:31,750
Hey, pops.

77
00:05:31,790 --> 00:05:34,210
I ain't that old yet, kid. What's up?

78
00:05:34,330 --> 00:05:36,170
Can I ask you for a favor?

79
00:05:38,750 --> 00:05:40,920
So, what did you need?

80
00:05:41,830 --> 00:05:44,790
Whoa! These are albaherons!

81
00:05:44,790 --> 00:05:46,710
I was hoping you'd butcher them for me.

82
00:05:46,960 --> 00:05:49,040
There are just too many for me to handle.

83
00:05:49,170 --> 00:05:52,540
I'll give you two packs of meat
for each one you take care of.

84
00:05:52,580 --> 00:05:55,080
Really now? You sure?

85
00:05:55,290 --> 00:05:56,000
Yes!

86
00:05:57,290 --> 00:05:58,880
These aren't part of our food reserves.

87
00:05:59,170 --> 00:06:01,080
I need him to break down the carcasses
so I can sell the meat.

88
00:06:01,710 --> 00:06:06,330
I have to use something to earn those 50 gold
coins to get my family out of serfdom, after all.

89
00:06:06,830 --> 00:06:10,330
It would cost extra to have
a butcher in town do it, anyways.

90
00:06:10,830 --> 00:06:14,420
So it's better to just outsource the job here,
which also means fewer trips overall.

91
00:06:14,630 --> 00:06:16,380
Gotta make the most of my time!

92
00:06:19,420 --> 00:06:21,290
Are you guys sure about this?

93
00:06:21,290 --> 00:06:24,540
Absolutely. We already
pulled it off once. Don't freak out.

94
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:29,290
By gradually adding new people to the team,
we'll eventually have enough to make two groups.

95
00:06:29,290 --> 00:06:31,330
That should double the
amount of boars we can hunt.

96
00:06:31,880 --> 00:06:36,080
But I wish I knew why the baron
was so hung up on having more boars.

97
00:06:36,330 --> 00:06:40,170
I don't get the impression his territory
is suffering from food shortages.

98
00:06:40,170 --> 00:06:42,080
Boar incoming!

99
00:06:44,580 --> 00:06:45,380
Brace yourselves!

100
00:06:46,920 --> 00:06:47,880
Attack now!

101
00:06:50,670 --> 00:06:52,170
Get over here, newbies!

102
00:07:01,830 --> 00:07:04,880
I can feel it! Another Trial of the Gods complete!

103
00:07:04,880 --> 00:07:05,880
Same here!

104
00:07:05,880 --> 00:07:07,460
Wow! You're right!

105
00:07:07,790 --> 00:07:09,460
I feel so much stronger!

106
00:07:09,880 --> 00:07:10,580
Oh?

107
00:07:10,880 --> 00:07:13,380
YOUR EXP HAS REACHED THE MAX OF 2000/2000.

108
00:07:10,880 --> 00:07:13,380
YOU HAVE GONE UP TO LEVEL 3.

109
00:07:10,880 --> 00:07:13,380
HP HAS GONE UP BY 25

110
00:07:10,880 --> 00:07:13,380
MP HAS GONE UP BY 40

111
00:07:10,880 --> 00:07:13,380
ATTACK HAS GONE UP BY 14

112
00:07:10,880 --> 00:07:13,380
ENDURANCE HAS GONE UP BY 14

113
00:07:10,880 --> 00:07:13,380
AGILITY HAS GONE UP BY 26

114
00:07:10,880 --> 00:07:13,380
INTELLIGENCE HAS GONE UP BY 40

115
00:07:10,880 --> 00:07:13,380
LUCK HAS GONE UP BY 26

116
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:12,920
Hell yeah! My plan worked!

117
00:07:13,380 --> 00:07:16,080
YOU HAVE GONE UP TO LEVEL 3.

118
00:07:13,380 --> 00:07:15,290
And I even leveled up!

119
00:07:16,170 --> 00:07:17,540
Just before the fight...

120
00:07:19,960 --> 00:07:21,330
Go, Denka!

121
00:07:21,670 --> 00:07:26,880
My creatures can be summoned to any location
that I can mark by sight within a 50 meter radius.

122
00:07:28,420 --> 00:07:30,790
And as long as the boar attacks
one of my creatures,

123
00:07:30,790 --> 00:07:32,920
it's enough to count me
as a participant in the battle!

124
00:07:33,250 --> 00:07:35,040
YOU HAVE GONE UP TO LEVEL 3.

125
00:07:35,750 --> 00:07:39,670
All is grist when it comes to the mill!
That's the hardcore gamer mindset!

126
00:07:42,250 --> 00:07:43,670
Sorry, Denka.

127
00:07:44,210 --> 00:07:46,330
R.I.P.

128
00:07:47,540 --> 00:07:51,130
3 MONTHS LATER

129
00:07:48,540 --> 00:07:51,790
This world apparently shares the custom
of celebrating the start of the new year,

130
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:54,580
which led to me being invited
to the chieftain's residence for the first time.

131
00:07:54,830 --> 00:07:57,250
Those candies were yummy, huh, Allen?

132
00:07:57,250 --> 00:07:59,880
Totally! And we even got some gifts to take home.

133
00:08:00,330 --> 00:08:04,460
I assume this is supposed to be the reward
for successfully meeting the 15 boar quota.

134
00:08:05,790 --> 00:08:07,080
We're home!

135
00:08:07,080 --> 00:08:08,250
Ah, welcome back.

136
00:08:08,420 --> 00:08:10,170
Did you have a good time at the chieftain's place?

137
00:08:10,290 --> 00:08:13,880
Yep! You two should have come with us.

138
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:16,880
Sitting through all that pomp and circumstance
is a boring way to start the new year.

139
00:08:17,170 --> 00:08:18,920
Now, let's get this party started!

140
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:19,880
Mm-hmm!

141
00:08:23,710 --> 00:08:24,630
Yum!

142
00:08:32,830 --> 00:08:34,420
Does it taste good, Mash?

143
00:08:34,420 --> 00:08:36,580
Yeah! It's nummy, big brudder!

144
00:08:37,250 --> 00:08:38,500
Ain't that nice?

145
00:08:38,710 --> 00:08:41,380
So, did the chieftain
have anything to say about us?

146
00:08:41,540 --> 00:08:43,500
Yeah, he was really appreciative.

147
00:08:43,710 --> 00:08:47,420
Given how things are going, we shouldn't have
a problem meeting the quota of 20 boars this year.

148
00:08:48,130 --> 00:08:50,380
It's all thanks to Allen and his plan
to train the newbies.

149
00:08:51,540 --> 00:08:53,040
By the way, Allerino...

150
00:08:53,040 --> 00:08:53,750
Yes?

151
00:08:53,960 --> 00:08:58,630
Do my eyes deceive me, or is that
a special bottle of something behind you?

152
00:08:58,630 --> 00:09:00,830
Oh, this? It's liquor.

153
00:09:00,830 --> 00:09:02,710
The chieftain gave it to me as a gift.

154
00:09:05,790 --> 00:09:07,080
Hook, line, sinker.

155
00:09:07,210 --> 00:09:08,750
Now to reel 'em in.

156
00:09:08,750 --> 00:09:12,290
Oh, hey, Mash!
Want to do more spear training soon?

157
00:09:12,290 --> 00:09:13,250
Yeah!

158
00:09:13,250 --> 00:09:14,500
I wanna train, too!

159
00:09:14,790 --> 00:09:17,460
Forget it. You're already strong enough, Krena.

160
00:09:17,460 --> 00:09:19,920
We gotta nurture Mash
cuz he has the makings of a spear user.

161
00:09:19,920 --> 00:09:21,080
Oh yeah?

162
00:09:21,080 --> 00:09:21,670
What's the deal?

163
00:09:22,210 --> 00:09:23,130
Dunno.

164
00:09:23,380 --> 00:09:25,540
That's it. Like moths to the flame...

165
00:09:25,670 --> 00:09:26,880
Is something the matter?

166
00:09:27,080 --> 00:09:30,670
Well, ya know, since the chieftain
sent you home with that liquor...

167
00:09:30,750 --> 00:09:33,210
Yep! It was a gift he gave to me!

168
00:09:33,210 --> 00:09:34,580
Oh, come on!

169
00:09:34,960 --> 00:09:37,500
Let's not be silly now, kid.

170
00:09:37,670 --> 00:09:40,040
What's so silly? He gave it to me, so it's mine-

171
00:09:40,040 --> 00:09:42,330
But everybody knows
you're not old enough to drink it!

172
00:09:42,330 --> 00:09:43,420
Yeah, what he said!

173
00:09:43,580 --> 00:09:45,500
Well, shucks.

174
00:09:45,500 --> 00:09:48,210
I guess I'll let you have it,
but only if you beat me in a contest.

175
00:09:48,210 --> 00:09:49,040
A contest?!

176
00:09:49,130 --> 00:09:50,920
Huh? What do you mean?

177
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:52,540
You against the two of us?

178
00:09:52,540 --> 00:09:53,630
That's right.

179
00:09:53,960 --> 00:09:55,670
Fine by me. You're on!

180
00:09:55,880 --> 00:09:57,080
Wait, Gerda!

181
00:09:57,080 --> 00:09:58,330
Okay, but...

182
00:09:58,710 --> 00:10:01,040
What do I get from you if I win?

183
00:10:02,040 --> 00:10:04,670
Boo! Are you two really that stingy?

184
00:10:05,040 --> 00:10:07,250
Well, why don't you tell us what you want?

185
00:10:07,250 --> 00:10:08,830
If I win the contest...

186
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:11,460
you have to let me wield a spear
during all the boar hunts this year.

187
00:10:12,830 --> 00:10:16,630
We walked right into his trap.
He's a smart little cookie.

188
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:17,880
I'll be damned.

189
00:10:19,580 --> 00:10:20,540
All right.

190
00:10:21,040 --> 00:10:24,960
If we win, we get the liquor.
And if you win, you can fight in the boar hunts.

191
00:10:24,960 --> 00:10:25,960
No take-backs!

192
00:10:26,210 --> 00:10:27,250
Oh jeez...

193
00:10:27,250 --> 00:10:30,790
I don't see a problem with it.
We could use a little entertainment!

194
00:10:31,170 --> 00:10:33,830
So, what kind of contest did you have in mind?

195
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:35,210
Arm wrestling, of course!

196
00:10:35,210 --> 00:10:36,880
Arm wrestling?!

197
00:10:39,880 --> 00:10:41,000
Bring it on.

198
00:10:42,790 --> 00:10:45,960
Sorry, kid. But I ain't going easy on you.
Not with liquor on the line.

199
00:10:47,210 --> 00:10:50,630
I stocked my inventory
full of Fido cards just for this.

200
00:10:50,790 --> 00:10:52,330
All buffs into attack power!

201
00:10:52,630 --> 00:10:55,960
Not to mention, I'm level six now!
I've got this in the bag!

202
00:10:57,460 --> 00:10:58,330
Get ready...

203
00:10:58,960 --> 00:10:59,710
and go!

204
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:08,540
Whoa. What the-? Aw hell!

205
00:11:09,250 --> 00:11:11,580
Aw hell! Aw hell! Allen!

206
00:11:11,580 --> 00:11:13,170
Whoa there!

207
00:11:13,170 --> 00:11:15,210
Aaaaand BAM!

208
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:17,250
Dammit! I lost!

209
00:11:17,250 --> 00:11:18,630
You're so cool, Big brudder!

210
00:11:18,750 --> 00:11:20,880
Whew! That was a close one!

211
00:11:21,130 --> 00:11:26,290
From what I can tell, Gerda's attack stat
must be somewhere between 150 and 200.

212
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:30,420
Okay, Allen. I'll wait until
the soreness in your arm wears off.

213
00:11:35,040 --> 00:11:38,790
Oh, wow. I never realized
how calloused Dad's hands were...

214
00:11:39,290 --> 00:11:41,580
It's proof of how hard he works for us every day.

215
00:11:42,290 --> 00:11:43,960
So big and hulking.

216
00:11:44,960 --> 00:11:45,960
It's hard to believe.

217
00:11:46,420 --> 00:11:48,960
My son's old enough
to wanna compete with his old man.

218
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:52,710
The earlier you all treat me
like an adult, the better!

219
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:55,580
I've gotta put in a hundred times more effort
than everybody else!

220
00:11:56,080 --> 00:11:58,670
And it all starts with raising my stats
by leveling up!

221
00:11:59,330 --> 00:12:00,750
Okay, get ready...

222
00:12:01,330 --> 00:12:02,130
and go!

223
00:12:14,250 --> 00:12:16,000
Rodin takes it!

224
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:17,500
Aw yeah!

225
00:12:17,880 --> 00:12:19,250
Guess I've gotta take the L...

226
00:12:19,540 --> 00:12:22,580
His attack stat has to be over 300 at least!

227
00:12:23,500 --> 00:12:25,500
You win this one, Dad.

228
00:12:25,790 --> 00:12:26,830
Here. It's yours.

229
00:12:27,420 --> 00:12:27,830
Look.

230
00:12:27,830 --> 00:12:29,580
Hooray! Time to drink!

231
00:12:29,580 --> 00:12:30,540
Yeah!

232
00:12:32,130 --> 00:12:35,790
Considering their strength,
Gerda's attack stat is around D-rank.

233
00:12:35,790 --> 00:12:38,130
While Dad's is more like C-rank.

234
00:12:38,130 --> 00:12:42,880
That at least gives me a reference for how strong
the people playing on normal mode can get.

235
00:12:43,290 --> 00:12:45,540
You should know better
than to go so hard on a child!

236
00:12:45,710 --> 00:12:48,080
Don't let it get you down, Allen.

237
00:12:48,290 --> 00:12:48,790
Huh?

238
00:12:49,210 --> 00:12:51,000
Oh, I guess they thought I looked upset.

239
00:12:51,290 --> 00:12:54,210
They're right. You're not weak by any means.

240
00:12:54,210 --> 00:12:56,040
I'm just too strong is all!

241
00:12:56,420 --> 00:12:59,380
But you're not hunting any boars
until you have what it takes to beat me!

242
00:13:00,080 --> 00:13:01,790
Nice. I'm gonna hold him to that.

243
00:13:01,960 --> 00:13:05,130
I stand a decent shot of making that happen
if I can get to summon level four before fall!

244
00:13:05,380 --> 00:13:08,040
Okay, Dad. I'll give up on hunting for now!

245
00:13:08,040 --> 00:13:09,670
But I'll beat you eventually!

246
00:13:10,710 --> 00:13:13,170
Hey, Mathilda! We need more snackage!

247
00:13:13,170 --> 00:13:15,670
You two better give it a rest!

248
00:13:15,670 --> 00:13:18,460
C'mon, it's the new year! Let me have my fun!

249
00:13:18,750 --> 00:13:20,790
Just bring me something to snack on, already!

250
00:13:23,420 --> 00:13:25,040
Okay. You were saying?

251
00:13:25,460 --> 00:13:26,500
Nothing.

252
00:13:27,750 --> 00:13:31,000
Mathilda might lowkey have C-rank stats, too...

253
00:13:31,960 --> 00:13:36,000
THE HARDCORE GAMER DOMINATES

254
00:13:31,960 --> 00:13:36,000
IN ANOTHER WORLD WITH GARBAGE BALANCING

255
00:13:36,380 --> 00:13:39,460
ALLEN - AGE 7

256
00:13:36,380 --> 00:13:39,460
JUNE

257
00:13:36,920 --> 00:13:39,790
My summon level finally went up again!

258
00:13:39,460 --> 00:13:43,420
ENHANCE SKILL HAS REACHED

259
00:13:39,460 --> 00:13:43,420
THE MAX EXP OF 100000/100000.

260
00:13:39,460 --> 00:13:43,420
YOU HAVE REACHED ENHANCE LEVEL 4.

261
00:13:39,460 --> 00:13:43,420
YOU HAVE REACHED SUMMMON LEVEL 4.

262
00:13:39,460 --> 00:13:43,420
YOU HAVE REACHED GRIMOIRE EXPANSION LEVEL 3.

263
00:13:39,460 --> 00:13:43,420
YOU HAVE OBTAINED THE STORAGE SKILL.

264
00:13:40,250 --> 00:13:42,630
That's a lot of new info.

265
00:13:43,420 --> 00:13:45,790
Better check my stats page.

266
00:13:46,460 --> 00:13:50,500
Oh! I've unlocked E-rank summon creatures!
And even a new type!

267
00:13:50,710 --> 00:13:54,330
Seems I have to fuse them together again
to find out what kind exactly.

268
00:13:54,330 --> 00:13:58,130
But I have plenty of MP to spare this time,
so I can experiment freely!

269
00:13:58,460 --> 00:14:00,920
My card inventory went up by 10, too!

270
00:14:01,380 --> 00:14:04,580
The amount of buffs that summon creatures
provide scale by their level,

271
00:14:04,580 --> 00:14:08,670
so I should get a significant boost
if I fill my inventory with 40 E-rank cards.

272
00:14:09,170 --> 00:14:11,920
I can totally beat Dad at arm wrestling now!

273
00:14:13,080 --> 00:14:15,580
STORAGE

274
00:14:13,830 --> 00:14:15,040
"Storage"?

275
00:14:15,580 --> 00:14:18,380
No level number next to it,
so it must be a fixed skill?

276
00:14:22,130 --> 00:14:24,250
Uh... is that a hole?

277
00:14:26,210 --> 00:14:27,710
Coming through!

278
00:14:28,630 --> 00:14:29,920
Seems pretty deep.

279
00:14:33,670 --> 00:14:35,330
I didn't hear it hit the bottom...

280
00:14:39,920 --> 00:14:42,080
Ah! It's the stone I threw in earlier.

281
00:14:41,790 --> 00:14:46,580
ITEM OVERVIEW

282
00:14:41,790 --> 00:14:46,580
STONE: 1 COUNT

283
00:14:42,460 --> 00:14:45,880
So, I can call up a mental image
of the items I've stored, huh?

284
00:14:46,630 --> 00:14:48,250
Okay. Time to experiment!

285
00:14:48,830 --> 00:14:50,420
Yeet. Yeet.

286
00:14:50,790 --> 00:14:52,500
Yeet! Yeet! Yeet! Yeet!

287
00:14:52,630 --> 00:14:58,750
ITEM OVERVIEW

288
00:14:52,630 --> 00:14:58,750
STONE: 200 COUNT

289
00:14:52,630 --> 00:14:58,750
FIREWOOD:

290
00:14:52,630 --> 00:14:58,750
WATER:

291
00:14:53,080 --> 00:14:56,290
Okay, so, I can put anything
in this hole as long as it fits.

292
00:14:56,290 --> 00:14:58,290
No limits on the amount, either.

293
00:14:59,330 --> 00:15:02,380
Weird. This feels very wrong.

294
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:08,420
One major aspect of games
is how many items the player can hold.

295
00:15:09,290 --> 00:15:14,290
So why are they giving me a god-tier storage skill
at this particular point in time?

296
00:15:15,210 --> 00:15:18,580
Whether it's a key, a boat, or a magic carpet...

297
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:22,500
items are usually obtained
around the time they become necessary.

298
00:15:23,040 --> 00:15:25,460
Why? Because that's how
the devs design it, of course.

299
00:15:26,170 --> 00:15:28,790
Is something wrong, Allen? You're so quiet.

300
00:15:28,790 --> 00:15:30,880
Oh, nothing! I'm fine.

301
00:15:31,330 --> 00:15:33,460
There must be a reason behind this.

302
00:15:33,750 --> 00:15:36,380
Something that makes it necessary
to have right now.

303
00:15:38,250 --> 00:15:41,170
Time to play around with the E-rank summons.

304
00:15:41,170 --> 00:15:43,040
Let's go! Create: Insect E!

305
00:15:44,080 --> 00:15:45,540
Huh? Why didn't it work?

306
00:15:45,960 --> 00:15:47,500
Do I not have enough MP?

307
00:15:48,170 --> 00:15:50,040
But I just recovered it back to full...

308
00:15:51,580 --> 00:15:53,790
YOU DO NOT HAVE ENOUGH E-RANK MAGIC STONES

309
00:15:51,580 --> 00:15:53,790
TO CREATE INSECT E.

310
00:15:53,790 --> 00:15:55,380
M-magic stones?!

311
00:15:55,380 --> 00:15:58,040
So creating E-ranks requires items now?

312
00:15:58,040 --> 00:16:00,380
Um, let's see. Where can I get some?

313
00:16:00,750 --> 00:16:01,380
Ah!

314
00:16:05,710 --> 00:16:08,420
With all the stealth of a ninja...

315
00:16:13,080 --> 00:16:16,210
Stored in this bag with all the money
I've earned lately...

316
00:16:20,670 --> 00:16:23,960
I kept some magic stones from the horned rabbits
that wandered into the village.

317
00:16:24,330 --> 00:16:26,250
Being a hoarder pays off!

318
00:16:28,420 --> 00:16:30,250
Okay. Take two.

319
00:16:30,750 --> 00:16:32,290
Create: Insect E!

320
00:16:33,130 --> 00:16:34,170
Bruh.

321
00:16:34,250 --> 00:16:37,960
YOU DO NOT HAVE ENOUGH E-RANK MAGIC STONES

322
00:16:34,250 --> 00:16:37,960
TO CREATE INSECT E.

323
00:16:34,830 --> 00:16:37,540
I'm literally holding an E-rank magic stone.

324
00:16:38,040 --> 00:16:39,750
Oh, right. I should put it in storage.

325
00:16:40,710 --> 00:16:41,580
Yeet!

326
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:44,460
And now, take three. Create: Insect E!

327
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:48,380
There we go! Guess that's what
I'm supposed to use storage for.

328
00:16:45,580 --> 00:16:48,790
INSECT E

329
00:16:45,580 --> 00:16:48,790
ENDURANCE +10 AGILITY +10

330
00:16:48,790 --> 00:16:50,880
INSECT E

331
00:16:50,290 --> 00:16:52,330
Looks like the E-rank insect is a butterfly.

332
00:16:50,880 --> 00:16:52,750
ENDURANCE +10 AGILITY +10

333
00:16:52,750 --> 00:16:54,460
Come on out, little fella!

334
00:16:57,380 --> 00:16:59,000
Whoa! You ain't little!

335
00:16:59,000 --> 00:16:59,710
Allen?

336
00:16:59,710 --> 00:17:00,250
Oh crap!

337
00:17:00,580 --> 00:17:01,500
Hide!

338
00:17:01,750 --> 00:17:04,170
I'm boned. She's gonna notice for sure!

339
00:17:04,330 --> 00:17:06,710
What's the matter? I heard you shouting.

340
00:17:06,710 --> 00:17:10,170
Oh, uhhh... I was like shazam!
And then yowza! Big surprise!

341
00:17:10,170 --> 00:17:12,330
What does that even mean? You're such a goofball.

342
00:17:18,290 --> 00:17:20,460
No idea why that worked, but thank God.

343
00:17:22,420 --> 00:17:25,460
Butterfly! Butterfly!

344
00:17:25,460 --> 00:17:27,460
Magic stones in the sk- argh!

345
00:17:37,960 --> 00:17:40,460
My own summon nearly scared the pants off me.

346
00:17:40,960 --> 00:17:43,500
So, Beast E is a saber-toothed tiger, huh?

347
00:17:43,630 --> 00:17:46,000
Seems bigger and tougher than my dog summon!

