BIRD E

413
00:19:42,330 --> 00:19:45,670
And now, I've created all of the E-rank summons
available!

414
00:19:46,290 --> 00:19:49,250
Alright. Let's find out what kind
of abilities they have!

415
00:19:54,580 --> 00:19:55,630
What's wrong, Hawkins?

416
00:19:58,460 --> 00:19:59,830
Ouch!

417
00:20:03,210 --> 00:20:04,500
Thanks, Beanzie!

418
00:20:08,880 --> 00:20:09,630
Papillon!

419
00:20:16,380 --> 00:20:17,540
Sic 'em, Tama!

420
00:20:24,500 --> 00:20:25,880
Hell yeah!

421
00:20:39,460 --> 00:20:41,130
You rock, Wally!

422
00:20:45,380 --> 00:20:47,830
Wally? Tama?! Papillon?!

423
00:20:50,250 --> 00:20:51,670
Did I just hallucinate that?

424
00:20:55,290 --> 00:21:00,960
For these past seven years, I've been considering
exactly how a Summoner is supposed to play.

425
00:21:01,580 --> 00:21:04,540
I could read a game FAQ or walkthrough
for any other game,

426
00:21:04,790 --> 00:21:06,880
but that isn't an option here.

427
00:21:07,920 --> 00:21:12,170
I have to figure out how to tap
into a Summoner's full potential all by myself.

428
00:21:13,130 --> 00:21:18,250
At this point, I'm convinced that each summon type
is designed to fulfill a specific role in battle.

429
00:21:20,250 --> 00:21:21,460
Come on out, everybody!

